    S:gt.blockmachines.componentassemblyline.name=Component Assembly Line
    S:gt.blockmachines.componentassemblyline.tooltip=Machine Type: §eHigh-Capacity Component Assembler, CoAL§r\nAssembles basic components (motors, pumps, etc.) in large batches\nThe §l§eComponent Assembly Line Casing §r§7limits the recipes the machine can perform. See the NEI pages for details\nUsing casings above the required recipe tier provides a speed bonus:\n§eHalves recipe time per tier above recipe\n§oMuch more efficient than other competing brands!\n§aSupports Multi-Amp and Laser Hatches!\nThis machine can run recipes regardless of tier, if given enough energy\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\nHold §l[LSHIFT]§r§7 to display structure guidelines\nAdded by: §a§bMadMan310§r§7
    S:gt.blockmachines.componentassemblyline.tooltip_secondary=§fDimensions: §633§7x§69§7x§610§7 (§6L§7x§6W§7x§6H§7) §c(Hollow)\n§fStructure: \n   §fController: §7Front center, 8th layer\n   §6516-646 §fAdvanced Iridium Plated Machine Casing\n   §6280 §fUV+ Tiered Glass\n   §6126 §fPBI Pipe Casing\n   §6124 §fAdvanced Filter Casing\n   §655 §fAssembly Line Casing\n   §643 §fComponent Assembly Line Casing §b(Tiered)\n   §630 §fAssembler Machine Casing\n   §62-4 §fTungstensteel Frame Box\n   §e1+ §fEnergy Hatch: §7Any outer iridium casing on the 2nd to top layer\n   §e1 §fMaintenance Hatch: §7Any casing around controller\n   §e1-8 §fInput Bus: §7Any casing or frame box at front of conveyor belt\n   §e0+ §fInput Hatch: §7Any side bottom edge casing\n   §e1+ §fOutput Bus: §7Any casing at end of conveyor belt\n   \nSubchannel §bglass§7 determines §bGlass Tier\nSubchannel §bcomponent_casing§7 determines §bComponent Assembly Line Casing Tier\n§7§m------------------------------\n§fUse the Multiblock Structure §9Hologram §1Projector§f to visualize/build the structure!
