    S:gt.blockmachines.extremeheatexchanger.name=Extreme Heat Exchanger
    S:gt.blockmachines.extremeheatexchanger.tooltip=Machine Type: §eHeat Exchanger, EHE§r\nInputs are §cLava§7, §cHot Coolant§7, §cHot Solar Salt§7, or §cPlasma\nOutputs are §9Pahoehoe Lava§7, §9IC2 Coolant§7, §9Cold Solar Salt§7, or §9Molten Metal\nConverts distilled water into §rSH Steam§7 or §rSC Steam§7 in the process\nOutputs §rSC Steam§7 if the input rate of hot fluid is above a certain §dthreshold\nExplodes immediately if it runs out of distilled water\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\n§cLava§7 | SC Threshold §d80,000 L/s§7 | Max Input §c160,000 L/s§7 | Max Output §r640,000 L/t SC Steam\n§cHot Coolant§7 | SC Threshold §d8,000 L/s§7 | Max Input §c128,000 L/s§7 | Max Output §r1,280,000 L/t SC Steam\n§cHot Solar Salt§7 | SC Threshold §d1,600 L/s§7 | Max Input §c3,200 L/s§7 | Max Output §r160,000 L/t SC Steam\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\n§cPlasma§7 always outputs §rDense SC Steam§7 regardless of input rate\nThe max input and output rates depend on the plasma's density (EU/L)\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\nA circuit in the controller lowers the SC threshold at the cost of steam\n§d-150 L/s§7 SC Threshold and §r-1.5%§7 steam output per circuit over 1\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\nHold §l[LSHIFT]§r§7 to display structure guidelines
    S:gt.blockmachines.extremeheatexchanger.tooltip_secondary=§fDimensions: §611§7x§65§7x§66§7 (§6L§7x§6W§7x§6H§7) \n§fStructure: \n   §fController: §7Front bottom center\n   §625-120 §fRobust Tungstensteel Machine Casing\n   §672 §fEV+ Tiered Glass\n   §660 §fTungstensteel Pipe Casing\n   §648 §fPressure Resistant Wall\n   §e1 §fMaintenance Hatch: §7Any casing\n   §e2+ §fInput Hatch: §7Front center casing (hot fluid), any bottom casing (distilled water)\n   §e2+ §fOutput Hatch: §7Back center casing (cool fluid), any top casing (steam)\n   \nSubchannel §bglass§7 determines §bGlass Tier\n§7§m------------------------------\n§fUse the Multiblock Structure §9Hologram §1Projector§f to visualize/build the structure!
    S:gt.blockmachines.fix.name.remover.name=Name Remover
    S:gt.blockmachines.fix.name.remover.tooltip=Removes various NBT tags as well as covers.\n \n§nFirst Slot§r\nThe item you want to strip of NBT\n \n§nSecond Slot§r\nOne of the following circuits:\n§lCircuit 1:§r  Attempt to fix broken ores by removing the Display Name tag\n§lCircuit 3:§r  Remove Railcraft stacking tag\n§lCircuit 4:§r  Remove Anvil repair tag\n§lCircuit 5:§r  Remove Dye from Leather armor\n§lCircuit 6:§r  Remove Spray color from GT items\n§lCircuit 7:§r  Remove Muffler Upgrade from GT machines\n§lCircuit 24:§r  Remove everything including covers. Be careful you won't recover the covers!\n \n§lNo Circuit:§r Remove everything except covers
