    S:gt.blockmachines.neutronactivator.name=Neutron Activator
    S:gt.blockmachines.neutronactivator.tooltip=Machine Type: §eNeutron Activator, NA§r\nSuperluminal-velocity Motion.\nThe minimum height of the Speeding Pipe Casing is 4\nPer extra Speeding Pipe Casing will give time discount\nBut it will reduce the Neutron Accelerator efficiency\nYou need to input energy to the Neutron Accelerator to get it running\nIt will output correct products with Specific Neutron Kinetic Energy\nOtherwise it will output trash\nThe Neutron Kinetic Energy will decrease 72KeV/s when no Neutron Accelerator is running\nInputting Graphite/Beryllium dust can reduce 10MeV per dust immediately.\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\nHold §l[LSHIFT]§r§7 to display structure guidelines
    S:gt.blockmachines.neutronactivator.tooltip_secondary=§fDimensions: §65§7x§65§7x§66-256§7 (§6L§7x§6W§7x§6H§7) \n§fStructure: \n   §fController: §7Front bottom center\n   §e1+ §fNeutron Accelerator: §7Any bottom edge casing\n   §e0+ §fNeutron Sensor: §7Any bottom edge casing\n   §e1 §fMaintenance Hatch: §7Any bottom edge casing\n   §e1+ §fInput Bus/Hatch: §7Any top edge casing\n   §e1+ §fOutput Bus/Hatch: §7Any bottom edge casing\n   \n   §9Base Structure\n   §632 §fAny Tiered Glass\n   §67-27 §fClean Stainless Steel Machine Casing\n   §618 §fProcessor Machine Casing\n   §616 §fSteel Frame Box\n   §64 §fSpeeding Pipe Casing\n   \n   §9Each Additional §bLayer\n   §68 §fAny Tiered Glass\n   §64 §fSteel Frame Box\n   §61 §fSpeeding Pipe Casing\n   \nProjector stack size determines §bHeight\nSubchannel §bglass§7 determines §bGlass Tier\n§7§m------------------------------\n§fUse the Multiblock Structure §9Hologram §1Projector§f to visualize/build the structure!
    S:gt.blockmachines.nuclearsaltprocessingplant.controller.tier.single.name=Nuclear Salt Processing Plant
    S:gt.blockmachines.nuclearsaltprocessingplant.controller.tier.single.tooltip=Machine Type: §eReactor Processing Unit, Cold Trap, NSPP§r\n§62§7 Parallels per §fVoltage§7 Tier\n§a250%§7 Speed\n§8100%§7 EU Usage\nProcesses depleted nuclear salts that come from the LFTR\nHandles the recipes of the Reactor Processor Unit and Cold Trap\nOnly Thermally Insulated Casings can be replaced with hatches\nMufflers on top, Energy Hatches on bottom, exactly 2 of each are required\nMaintenance Hatch goes on the back, opposite of the controller block\nInputs go on the left side of the multi, outputs on the right side\n§5500 §7Pollution per second\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\nHold §l[LSHIFT]§r§7 to display structure guidelines
    S:gt.blockmachines.nuclearsaltprocessingplant.controller.tier.single.tooltip_secondary=§fDimensions: §63§7x§69§7x§65§7 (§6L§7x§6W§7x§6H§7) §c(Hollow)\n§fStructure: \n   §fController: §7Front center, 3rd layer\n   §658 §fIV Machine Casing\n   §60-32 §fThermally Insulated Casing\n   §e2 §fEnergy Hatch: §7Bottom insulated casings\n   §e1 §fMaintenance Hatch: §7Casing behind controller\n   §e2 §fMuffler Hatch: §7Top insulated casings\n   §e0+ §fInput Bus: §7Any left side insulated casing\n   §e0+ §fInput Hatch: §7Any left side insulated casing\n   §e0+ §fOutput Bus: §7Any right side insulated casing\n   §e0+ §fOutput Hatch: §7Any right side insulated casing\n§7§m------------------------------\n§fUse the Multiblock Structure §9Hologram §1Projector§f to visualize/build the structure!
